damaged_code:
```rust
struct Range {
    begin: i32,
    end: i32, // exclusive
}

impl Range {
    fn overlaps_with(&self, other: &Range) -> bool {
        // Buggy overlap logic: misses enclosure cases and miscalculates boundaries
        (self.begin >= other.begin && self.begin <= other.end) ||
        (self.end >= other.begin && self.end <= other.end)
    }
}
```

counterexample:
Writing range overlap by checking the negation of non-overlapping states:
```rust
impl Range {
    fn overlaps_with(&self, other: &Range) -> bool {
        !(self.end <= other.begin || self.begin >= other.end)
    }
}
```

fix:
Express range overlap elegantly by checking the negation of the two scenarios where they *cannot* overlap: one ends before the other begins, or vice versa.
```rust
struct Range {
    begin: i32,
    end: i32,
}

impl Range {
    fn overlaps_with(&self, other: &Range) -> bool {
        // They end before we begin OR they begin after we end
        if other.end <= self.begin { return false; }
        if other.begin >= self.end { return false; }
        true
    }
}
```
